{"author":{"id":"98a8d196af4b3b3a11b496a622c3857deea61c7fcfd81ca5bb36f1f18227ef6b"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1795282649,"nonce":"Byl3qTLYLWd5t8TaKisFr7HkPbw=","title":"Build the playable prototype of step 1 in this repository","message":"\u003e Create a prototype based on current draft files.\n\n\u003e All dependencies managed through mise, where it makes sense, even rust 1.100 if it makes sense.\n\n## Goal\n\nA person can play step 1 of design.md from this repository, alone and on a LAN. A playtest can then answer the question of the design: is it fun to chase a plane and shoot it apart?\n\n## What the drafts take as true\n\nThe three drafts describe a prototype as built and proven. This repository holds no code yet. The code that the drafts measured is in an earlier checkout, outside this repository. Thus each standing of \"Proven\" in requirements.md is a claim about that checkout until this repository shows it again.\n\n## Steps\n\nThe child issues hold the steps. A comment on this issue lists them. The order follows the game-design method: the rules first, then one playable loop, then one system at a time.\n\n## Out of scope\n\nSteps 2 to 5 of design.md: effects and sound, replay and spectators, a GPU simulation, and the stretch goals. Generated assets. Camera input.\n\nAgent: Claude Fable 5.2","files":null}]}